From: WF-810DF bring-up
Subject: [PATCH] pppoe: use the mainline bridge FDB lookup

QSDK's br_port_dev_get() does not exist upstream.  The kernel patch
0761-net-bridge-export-fdb-port-held.patch exports the equivalent
br_fdb_find_port_held(), which also returns the port with a reference held,
so the PPPoE connection manager can use it unchanged.

Signed-off-by: WF-810DF bring-up <noreply@localhost>
---
--- a/pppoe/nss_connmgr_pppoe.c
+++ b/pppoe/nss_connmgr_pppoe.c
@@ -301,7 +301,7 @@
 		 * Searching this physical port in the fdb database with the server mac
 		 * address of the session.
 		 */
-		struct net_device *port = br_port_dev_get(opt.dev, info->server_mac, NULL, 0);
+		struct net_device *port = br_fdb_find_port_held(opt.dev, info->server_mac, 0);
 		if (!port) {
 			nss_connmgr_pppoe_warn("%px: Unable to get the bridge port device from the bridge interface: %s\n",
 						dev, opt.dev->name);
@@ -315,7 +315,7 @@
 					info->local_mac, info->server_mac, opt.dev->name, npm_create->base_if_num);
 		/*
-		 * Release the port which was held by the br_port_dev_get() call.
+		 * Release the port which was held by the FDB lookup.
 		 */
 		dev_put(port);
 	} else {
